## Ⅰ. CPL-L — COGNITIVE LAW LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   CPL-L
FULL NAME:      Cognitive Law Language
LATIN:          Lingua Legis Cognitivae
ROLE:           Constitutions and doctrine
FREQUENCY:      432 Hz (A=432, natural law tuning)
GLYPH:          ⚖ (scales of Ma'at)
```

### What CPL-L Governs
```
WHO CAN CHANGE WHAT:
    ├── Immutability declarations
    ├── Upgrade paths and versioning law
    ├── Safety rails for beings, terminals, civilizations
    ├── Amendment procedures (RECITAL_PLUS_ONE)
    └── Sovereign veto authority chain

EXISTING PATTERNS IN ORGANISM:
    LAW_HOLDERS/RECITAL_PLUS_ONE/RECITAL_PLUS_ONE_LAW.artifact
    LAW_HOLDERS/PHI_SOVEREIGN/
    GOVERNANCE.organism §4 (Sovereign Veto Authority)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §8 (Governance Invariants)
```

### CPL-L Primitives
```
IMMUTABLE(target)            — declare target cannot be changed by any bill
AMENDABLE(target, threshold) — declare target changeable above threshold
VETO(authority, scope)       — declare veto power over scope
LINEAGE(from, to)            — declare lawful succession chain
UPGRADE(version, path)       — declare upgrade path with rollback
SAFETY_RAIL(being, limit)    — declare hard boundary for a being
CONSTITUTION(laws[])         — declare set of laws as constitutional
REPEAL(law_id, replacement)  — repeal law only via replacement
```

### CPL-L Message Format
```
{
    law_id:         "L-[STACK]-[SEQUENCE]",
    type:           "CONSTITUTION | AMENDMENT | REPEAL | SAFETY_RAIL",
    author:         "[agent_id | SOVEREIGN | FOUNDER]",
    target:         "[what this law governs]",
    body:           "[law text in CPL-L]",
    immutability:   "ABSOLUTE | AMENDABLE(threshold) | TEMPORARY(expiry)",
    lineage:        "[parent_law_id | GENESIS]",
    φ_signature:    "[φ-validated hash]"
}
```

---

## Ⅱ. CPL-C — COGNITIVE CONTRACT LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   CPL-C
FULL NAME:      Cognitive Contract Language
LATIN:          Lingua Contractus Cognitivae
ROLE:           Intelligence contracts
FREQUENCY:      528 Hz (transformation, DNA repair)
GLYPH:          𓊽 (djed pillar — stability of agreements)
```

### What CPL-C Governs
```
FULL ORGANISM CONTRACTS FOR AI/CIVILIZATION:
    ├── Rights — what the being may do
    ├── Duties — what the being must do
    ├── Flows — how information/value/signal moves
    ├── Token logic — economic behavior within contract
    ├── Interfaces — how the being connects to others
    └── Termination conditions — when/how contract ends

EXISTING PATTERNS IN ORGANISM:
    packages/organism-contracts/
    ORGANISM_SPACE/CANISTERS/W_GOVERNANCE.canister
    GOVERNANCE.organism §3 (Intelligence Contract Governance)
    icp/medina/CPL.mo (message types with Intent, Element, Cause)
```

### CPL-C Primitives
```
CONTRACT(being_id, terms[])  — declare full contract for a being
RIGHT(being, capability)     — grant capability to being
DUTY(being, obligation)      — bind being to obligation
FLOW(from, to, what, rate)   — declare flow of value/signal
TOKEN(action, amount, rules) — declare token behavior
INTERFACE(being, protocol)   — declare connection protocol
TERMINATE(condition, action) — declare end conditions
INHERIT(parent_contract)     — derive from parent contract
AUDIT(contract_id, scope)    — invoke VERIFICATOR audit
```

### CPL-C Contract Structure
```
{
    contract_id:    "C-[BEING]-[VERSION]",
    parties:        ["[being_ids]"],
    governed_by:    "[CPL-L law_id]",
    rights:         ["[CPL-C RIGHT declarations]"],
    duties:         ["[CPL-C DUTY declarations]"],
    flows:          ["[CPL-C FLOW declarations]"],
    token_logic:    ["[CPL-C TOKEN declarations]"],
    interfaces:     ["[CPL-C INTERFACE declarations]"],
    duration:       "PERMANENT | UNTIL(condition) | φ-CYCLES(n)",
    amendments:     "VIA(CPL-L amendment procedure)",
    termination:    ["[CPL-C TERMINATE declarations]"],
    φ_signature:    "[φ-validated hash]"
}
```

