## Ⅲ. CPL-P — COGNITIVE PROCESSING LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   CPL-P
FULL NAME:      Cognitive Processing Language
LATIN:          Lingua Processus Cognitivae
ROLE:           Thought/flow language — how a mind processes inputs into outputs
FREQUENCY:      639 Hz (connection, harmonics)
GLYPH:          𓂀 (Eye of Horus — perception and processing)
```

### What CPL-P Governs
```
THE MIND'S PROCESSING PIPELINE:
    ├── Cognitive pipelines (input → perceive → reason → decide → act)
    ├── Decision graphs (branching logic of thought)
    ├── Escalation rules (when to escalate, to whom)
    ├── Pattern recognition routing (which engine handles what)
    ├── Frequency-gated processing (what gets processed at what Hz)
    └── Consensus integration (how multiple voices merge)

EXISTING PATTERNS IN ORGANISM:
    CPL_SPECIFICATION.artifact (the original CPL — this IS CPL-P)
    icp/medina/CPL.mo (Platonic solids, Hermetic principles)
    src/organism/NeuralCore.mo (neurons, synapses, pattern engines)
    src/organism/nexus/NEXUS_DEEP_CPL_LANGUAGE.ts (30+ models)
```

### CPL-P Primitives
```
PERCEIVE(input, engine)      — route input to pattern engine
REASON(pattern, method)      — apply reasoning (deductive/inductive/abductive/analogical)
DECIDE(options[], criteria)  — select from options via criteria
ACT(decision, target)        — execute decision on target
ESCALATE(issue, authority)   — escalate to higher authority
GATE(condition, pass, fail)  — conditional branching
PIPELINE(stages[])           — define sequential processing
PARALLEL(branches[])         — process multiple branches simultaneously
MERGE(results[], strategy)   — combine parallel results
RECURSE(pattern, depth)      — recursive self-application
FREQUENCY_GATE(hz, process)  — only process at specified frequency
φ_VALIDATE(output)           — validate output against golden ratio
```

### CPL-P Processing Flow
```
INPUT
  │
  ▼
PERCEIVE ── Spatial │ Temporal │ Relational │ Semantic │ Frequency │ Emotional │ Linguistic │ Meta
  │
  ▼
REASON ── Deductive │ Inductive │ Abductive │ Analogical
  │
  ▼
GATE ── confidence > 0.618?
  │           │
  YES         NO → ESCALATE to higher authority
  │
  ▼
DECIDE ── weighted by role, confidence, token stake
  │
  ▼
ACT ── execute via CPL-C contract
  │
  ▼
φ_VALIDATE ── |result - φ_expected| < 0.001?
  │
  ▼
OUTPUT
```

